<div class="signin-tip">
  <h3>On a phone?</h3>
  <p>If you have the OSM app (or OSM added to your home screen), your phone may open OSM there instead of in this browser, so the sign-in can't come back here. To stop that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>on Android, go to <strong>Settings → Apps → OSM</strong> (or whatever the OSM icon is called) <strong>→ Open by default</strong> and turn off <strong>Open supported links</strong>. On Samsung phones this screen is called <strong>Set as default</strong>.</li>
    <li>in Firefox (or Fennec), you can instead go to <strong>Settings → Open links in apps</strong> and choose <strong>Never</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Chrome doesn't have a setting like this, so if you use Chrome, change the OSM app's settings as above.</p>
  <p>Then try again here.</p>
</div>
